•  payload (the actual telemetry)
•  priority_tier (from Code 0)
Capillaries: The Sector Interface
When SensoryCore ingests friction=0.85, temp=63.0, it’s not just storing data. It’s oxygenating the packet — enriching it with meaning. The raw telemetry becomes brisket bark.
Veins: Feedback Loop
After processing, sectors push waste products back to the heart:
•  EmotionalCore sends thermal_drift (did the 37°C conduit hold?)
•  SensoryCore sends buffer_pressure (are we dropping packets?)
•  ARCHANGEL-12 sends consolidation_pulse (time to save?)
The Orchestrator reads these on the next tick and adjusts the next heartbeat. That’s homeostasis.
